NOTICE
======

This file records where everything in this repository came from, so that
anyone reading, forking or verifying the app can trace each part to its
source. It is written for a Quran application, where provenance matters more
than it does in ordinary software: a reader is entitled to know exactly how
the text in front of them was produced.


1. The Quranic text
-------------------

The Quranic text is the word of Allah, sent for all mankind. No claim of
ownership or licence is made over it by anyone, this project included.

What CAN be discussed in terms of rights is everything around it: the software,
the databases that describe the layout, the annotations, and the artwork. Those
are covered below.


2. Third-party data
-------------------

The database the app ships, `public/data/quran.sqlite`, is BUILT — it is not
transcribed by hand and contains no text typed by this project. Its inputs:

  Quranic Universal Library (QUL) — https://qul.tarteel.ai
    - "Indopak 16 lines layout"  ->  data/source/taj-indopak-16-lines.db
        Which words fall on which line of which page. This is the source of
        every line break in the app.
    - "Indopak Nastaleeq script — Word by Word"  ->  data/source/indopak-nastaleeq.db
        The word-by-word Indo-Pak text.
    - Metadata: surah names, ayah records, juz, ruku, rub, sajda, manzil, hizb
        ->  data/source/metadata/
    - The Indopak Nastaleeq font (Hanafi, with waqf lazmi)
        ->  public/fonts/indopak-nastaleeq.ttf

  alfurqan (npm)
    The Uthmani tajweed-annotated text, from which the per-letter tajweed rules
    are aligned onto the Indo-Pak script. Used by pipeline/lib/extract-source.js.

The two QUL source databases are gitignored, as third-party data. The built
`quran.sqlite` is committed so the app runs after `npm install`.


3. The printed edition
----------------------

The app models a specific printed copy:

    16-line Indo-Pak Mushaf, colour-coded tajweed
    Shan Maktaba Madina Printing Press, March 2011
    Text certified by six named qaris and two registered proof-readers of the
    Auqaf Department, Government of the Punjab

That copy was used in two different ways, and the distinction matters.

  (a) VERIFIED against it — facts, checked and recorded, not copied:
        - the offset between our page index and the printed page number
        - the page each of the 30 paras begins on (src/data/juzStart.ts)
        - the position, side, numbering and spacing of the ruku, sajdah and
          para-quarter marks
        - the content of the surah heading band and the page header
      These are statements of fact about a published book. They were determined
      by measurement and by reading the book, and are recorded as data.

  (b) COPIED from it — the publisher's own artwork:
        - public/img/makharij-upper.webp
        - public/img/makharij-lower.webp
      These are extracted, cropped and re-encoded from the makharij diagrams
      printed on page 552 of that edition. They are the publisher's
      illustrations, not scripture, and no licence to redistribute them has
      been sought or granted. See section 5.


